===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} *{{m|enm||tilȝer, *telȝer}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|telgor}}, {{m|ang|telgra}}, {{m|ang|telgre}} {{gloss|"twig, branch, shoot"}} (also {{m|ang|telga}}, {{m|ang|telge}} (whence {{l|en|tillow}})), from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*telgô}}, {{m|gem-pro|*telgǭ}}, {{m|gem-pro|*telguz||twig, branch}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*delgʰ-||to split, divide, cut, carve}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|telg||descendant, scion, offshoot, shoot}}, {{cog|nds-nl|telge||twig, branch}}, {{cog|de|Zelge||twig, branch, bough}}, {{cog|sv|telning||branch, scion, sapling}}, {{cog|is|tág||willow-twig}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|tillow}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A young [[tree]].
#: {{rfquotek|Evelyn}}
# A [[shoot]] of a [[plant]] which springs from the root or bottom of the original [[stalk]]; a [[sapling]]; a [[sucker]].

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To produce new [[shoot]]s from the root or from around the bottom of the original stalk; stool.

